# Shape: split origins. The server app owns the whole main domain; the owner
# UI is served by the second site block in infra/caddy/Caddyfile on
# MANTLE_CLIENT_SITE_ADDRESS (app.<domain>). Imported inside the main site
# block when MANTLE_CADDY_SHAPE=split. Needs the extra DNS record plus
# MANTLE_API_CORS_ORIGINS on the server. Release-owned; do not edit on a box.
#
# Caddy adds X-Forwarded-{For,Proto,Host} so the app can build correct
# absolute URLs and set secure cookies behind TLS. Wrapped in a handle so a
# conf.d drop-in's more specific handle still wins.
# Calls signalling (calls plan page 886126b4 section 4). The browser
# connects to wss://<site>/livekit (the LiveKit client appends /rtc itself);
# handle_path strips the prefix and Caddy proxies the WebSocket upgrade as
# is. Media never passes through Caddy (the livekit service publishes its
# own ports). With the `calls` profile off the upstream does not resolve
# and the path answers 502, which is right: there is no Call button then.
handle_path /livekit/* {
	reverse_proxy livekit:7880
}
handle {
	reverse_proxy web:3000
}
